    {
        "content": "<p>cfallin opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14254\">PR #14254</a> from <code>cfallin:u-mul-i-mul-we-all-mul-for-overflow</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This stacks on top of #14228, and adds the equivalent cases for multiplies.</p>\n<p>This required some new cases in the <code>ProducesFlags</code> enum because, at least on aarch64, the lowerings are a little more complex than a single multiply instruction that sets flags (no such instruction exists on that ISA). The canonical idiom is instead to compare the product (full width) against the product extended-from-narrow-width; or, for 64-bit x 64-bit multiplies, use the separate high-half multiply instruction and compare against zero. This requires either two (8/16/32-bit case) or three (64-bit case) instructions to do the multiply and produce a flag for the overflow case.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 620520209,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788235385
    },
