        "timestamp": 1788281239
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14254#discussion_r3906355911\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>At least in terms of indenting, I've found Emacs' builtin lisp formatting to be a reasonable default (and I guess we could always run Emacs in batch-mode with a little elisp script to do it) but the higher-level question of when to add linebreaks is one that is pretty variable, yeah...</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 620727719,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788281239
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> cfallin submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14254#pullrequestreview-5080742089\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 620728335,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788281369
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14254#discussion_r3906374753\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ah! I see what you mean -- the two results are independently computable with no overlap at all so we might as well have two separate lowerings and let them both fire. Yeah, I'll play with that.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 620728338,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788281370
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> cfallin submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14254#pullrequestreview-5081381842\">PR review</a>.</p>",
